 um  with those of influenza alien influenza  b and you can really see  the big difference that we had in the  number of circle v2 cases  uh and the influenza cases of the the  final flu season  and what was particularly remarkable is  that within a period of three weeks we  have  roughly the same number of stars for v2  cases as we had seen of  influenza throughout the six-month  seasonal influenza period between  november  of 2019 and april of 2020.  um so the  the initial uh interest that we had in  these cases were to look at  these very early cases um in the initial  pandemic peak so  we we knew that there was a very high  influx of novel cases in new york city  but we didn't know where these cases  actually originated from  so what we did is essentially expand  beyond the first two cases that we had  sequenced and do an analysis  of the first 84 cases that we encounter  in our health system  so we then did a very similar analysis  to the first two cases that i that i  showed earlier  and what that essentially told us is  that most of the initial cases that we  saw in our city  originated from europe approximately 80  percent  of the isolates that we had sequenced  were very similar to cases that  um that were also sequencing europe  during that time and what i told you  that  most of the initial introductions of the  virus in new york city  um were related to traverse between  europe and new york so this could be  tourists visiting new york but also  returning travelers  that returned to home in addition to the  introductions from europe we also saw  a small number of domestic introductions  so those were  mostly related to the initial cases that  were detected in the us  within washington saw sporadic cases  linked to the middle east and asia but  the really dominant introductions really  originated in europe the other striking  observation is that  we saw those cases all throughout the  city which meant that  the introduction of the virus was  equivalent  in