val  during a supervised quarantine so this  was  pcr testing which tests for the presence  of viral rna  and then liquids were only allowed to  enter in the basically tested  negative after week two of surveillance  so these uh we essentially followed for  this cohort  classes of 350 to 450 recruits that  arrived  weekly and we looked at a total of nine  classes  there were no interactions between  classes so each of them should be  quite well separated and then each of  the classes during the supervised  quarantine  i was instructed to use mask social  distancing to perform treatment hand  washing and each of the participants in  our study  was housed with a single roommate so  basically all um available public health  measures were  were taken to ensure that the risk of  transmission was reduced as much as  possible during the supervised  quarantine  so in total there were approximately  1800 study participants and these were  drawn from recruits  that mostly came from the east coast  as highlighted over here um  and then among the participants we saw  that  20 of them were positive for saraswati  on arrival for the supervised  quarantine and although the vast  majority 95 percent were asymptomatic  and this really highlights very clearly  especially in young adult cohorts  the need for widespread testing as many  of the cases  will will elude detection during  due to asymptomatic carriage um  then in a subsequent week so these the  first 20 participants were identified  upon arrival  in the subsequent two weeks we  identified another 31 participants that  tested positive  during their quarantine period and these  can either be specimens that were missed  on the initial screening  or they can signify transmission during  the two-week  quarantine of these  51 cases we identified genomes or we  obtained genomes for about 32  participants which is about  63 of the positive specimens  we then took those uh complete genomes  and we placed them  within the larger phylo