d accommodation  and sort of long-term shared rooms are  really important factor in sales machine  as well  so we have now taken some of those  lessons and have applied them  in our health system as well so we've  used similar approaches to  investigate multiple suspected  non-communal events uh starting an  august in august of 2020 um  we have identified multiple um noise  hormonal clusters and and  have been able to use genomic uh  analysis to precisely delineate whose  sparking was not part of these clusters  and again similar to the outbreak that  we had investigated in early 2019  it allows us to identify potential  exposure events  that precipitated some of these larger  outbreaks  with that i'll come to my conclusion so  with the data that i've shown today  um there is evidence from many multiple  introductions into the new york city  metropolitan area  um initial introductions were as early  as the end of january  although we did not think that these  initial introductions uh  resulted in forward spread based on the  fact that we only saw  a larger panamic peak towards the middle  of  may um  so the early transmission events that we  identified in the early communities  productively identified  mostly tracked back to cases that were  identified in europe and that indicates  that travelers from europe are  responsible for most of the initial  spreading  of sourceboard v2 in new york city but  over time these patterns have changed  quite considerably  and we think that these reflect patterns  in the different differences in the  patterns of international  domestic and local introductions that  also came with the opening up of the  city  as well as a continued community spread  that have shaped the viral landscape in  the city  we to track closely the emergence of new  mutations and variants of concern  which really requires a continuous  monitoring by genomic surveillance and  we see in particular for example the uk  variant and the b1.526 variant that are  fr